:"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T06:49:36-08:00","id":770698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dwight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/770264-ways-to-turn-mortal-into-spirits?p=770564#post770564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Idk I would probably go a little crazy after my mortal body dissipated and suddenly I find myself at the bottom of the spirit food chain doubt meditation would solve that.</div> </div> </div> </div>True<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/770264-ways-to-turn-mortal-into-spirits?p=770595#post770595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If 'mortals' includes Garou, very high ranking Uktena can learn 'Becoming Uktena.' That is a surefire way to become a very powerful spirit.<br /> <br /> I mean, you aren't whoever you were before, but that hardly matters because being a horned serpent is better anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Haha, love this and I agree<br /> <br /> Do you need a human/mortal to become a spirit? Or would a spirit posing as a mortal suffice through the materialise charm be enough for your needs perhaps. <br /> <br /> I imagine a whole new stange and terrifying world would await a human becoming a spirit. What type of spirit would they be? Which of their traits most determines their spiritual correspondence? What brood will the fall under? Will banes and the wyrm and weaver be after them? Will a garou bind them to something in an attempt to keep them from harm until they can be returned to mortality? Can the y ever go bacl? Will they become a snack for another spirit or umbral denizen? <br /> <br /> It's doable, in that anything in within the realms of imagination, but whats the why? What's the need and hope in the doing so?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T13:07:33-08:00","id":770908,"title":"","content":"Such a thing could probably be doable with a high-level Mystic Rite, I'd peg it at a 4 or maybe 5, performed in the Umbra. As others have mentioned, it's not the turning a mortal into a spirit that's the hard part, it's making them a viable part of the spiritual ecosystem that is tricky. Use a Rite as the handwavium for giving them decent Gnosis/Rage/Willpower/Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8485,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","user":"Random_Interrupt","date":". 11-21-2015, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T14:35:49-08:00","id":770959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/770264-ways-to-turn-mortal-into-spirits?p=770698#post770698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> True<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Haha, love this and I agree<br /> <br /> Do you need a human/mortal to become a spirit? Or would a spirit posing as a mortal suffice through the materialise charm be enough for your needs perhaps.<br /> <br /> I imagine a whole new stange and terrifying world would await a human becoming a spirit. What type of spirit would they be? Which of their traits most determines their spiritual correspondence? What brood will the fall under? Will banes and the wyrm and weaver be after them? Will a garou bind them to something in an attempt to keep them from harm until they can be returned to mortality? Can the y ever go bacl? Will they become a snack for another spirit or umbral denizen?<br /> <br /> It's doable, in that anything in within the realms of imagination, but whats the why? What's the need and hope in the doing so?</div> </div> </div> </div>(Just using our post as a jumping-off point -- only addressing it tangentially as a point of reference for certain aspects...)<br /> <br /> The thing about a question like this is that is &quot;jumps the fence&quot;, meta-physically speaking, into another splat's yard: the metaphysics involved in transforming an ordinary mortal into a spirit (of the Middle-Umbra variety) is something that -- should a Garou ever be interested in having happen, for whatever reasons -- would require seeking out a mage or powerful hedge-wizard to accomplish (more so the former than the latter, of course). While circumstances that the Garou, in general, face and interact with can <i>circumstantially </i>possibly lead to a given mortal becoming a spirit (perhaps as the by-product of having remained for years in a Middle Umbral realm, such as Avalon or similar, for example, without some mystical connection/projection against becoming wholly spirit/discorporated), it generally is beyond the purview of most Gifts/Rites for such a thing to be made to happen. (A mage, of course, could do so with Spirit:3/4, Life:3/4, Mind:3, Prime:1; Spirit/Life: transforms the target into an ephemeral being, in toto, while Mind helps guide the mental transition that would be a part of that process as well as allow the new spirit to cognitize things in a different manner; Prime would allow for the mortal-cum-spirit to retain a metaphysical sense of his essential self, metaphysically speaking, which in turn allows for potential interaction with the physical world again with less... difficulty... in the future.)<br /> <br /> The only &quot;predictable&quot; circumstances wherein I could perceive such a thing falling within the workings/inclinations of most Garou is perhaps via Rank:5 Gift or Rite that &quot;blesses&quot; the mortal with a spiritual existence either after natural death or at the time of the mystical enactment. (This would, of course, be quite different from a mortal becoming a Wraith, as they'd become a Middle-Umbral-as-more-elemental essence, but would serve as some sort of very high reward for some truly great act, duty or sacrifice that would warrant such a shift -- or &quot;elevation&quot;, in the minds of most Garou -- for said mortal.)<br /> <br /> This would so rare, however, as to be the stuff of legends -- literally. It would be akin to a vampire achieving Golconda or a werewolf of the Croatan tribe coming back out of the Umbra, today, whole-and-complete and ready to revive his tribe, somehow. Rare, rare stuff....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-21T22:03:57-08:00","id":771223,"title":"","content":"Hmmmn... saw a reference to one of the Maeljin being a former mortal and was thinking it would be cool for some Wealthy and EVIL occultist to try undertaking a similar apotheosis...<br /> <br /> Oh speaking of mages?<br /> <br /> Been wondering... is it safe to say that if lhianian, or mortal with numina, enslaves a spirit... garou could get involved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img it