the building and the cycle begins again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:07:29-08:00","id":771487,"title":"","content":"Had an idea for a while... but not sure how to bring in evidence of it in play...<br /> <br /> A human who allys himself with garou and dies for it... bring in evidence he reincarnated as kinfolk, showing gaia IS Just where she can be.<br /> <br /> not sure how to bring it to PC's attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:26:54-08:00","id":771496,"title":"","content":"Children of gaia have a rite I believe that can turn worthy mortal of humainty into kinfolk bearing under spiritual and ritual blessings. <br /> <br /> Here we go:<br /> <br /> RITE OF THE PARTED VEIL (Children of Gaia Tribebook)<br /> <br /> The Children of Gaia sometimes adopt humans who bear no Garou blood as Kinfolk. This may occur when a Garou takes a mate; even then, the ritemaster makes extensive study of the subject prior to performing the rite to determine the subject's suitability. The ritual itself must be performed on three separate occasions, and when complete, the Veil is permanently pierced and the subject becomes immune to the Delirium. Unlike the Rending of the Veil, ritemasters warn that this must never be used to terrify the subject; it is a welcoming rite.<br /> <br /> This is also a level 5 Rite. So not known by many and probably only safely performable by a few highly renowned and dutiful ritemasters. Imo.<br /> <br /> hope it helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T08:36:10-08:00","id":771505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/770264-ways-to-turn-mortal-into-spirits?p=771440#post771440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which was not my intention, humanity in my view is more of a pawn or even in a way the food for the Triat. The Garou and by extension the rest of the Changing Breeds are just as guilty they knowingly perform acts that strengthen the Wyrm. The slum lord that keeps his property in disrepair, and fixes nothing including the heat in frigid winters is an asshole that is causing misery. This feeds the Wyrm and creates a breeding ground for banes. When the Garou sweep into the building and slaughter the new Formori then turn and leave. They are just as guilty. The slum lord will rent out the building and the cycle begins again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I got what you meant. Not humanity but individual humans so low and digusting to their own fellow kind and life in general the wyrm sat up paid attention and when they died forced them into serving the twisted and deplorable designs they had used in life. <br /> <br /> It's not humanitys doing. Just a few terrible individuals through humanitys history. Like it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T10:17:43-08:00","id":771576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/770264-ways-to-turn-mortal-into-spirits?p=771223#post771223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmn... saw a reference to one of the Maeljin being a former mortal and was thinking it would be cool for some Wealthy and EVIL occultist to try undertaking a similar apotheosis...</div> </div> </div> </div>I always thought this was a backhanded reference that the Maeljin Incarna were actually spectres, but that the specifics of their status allowed them limited involvement in the Middle Umbra. This possibly means that the Urge Wyrms are in fact Neverborn.<br /> <br /> The original books were seeded in all sorts of ways for crossover, but the gameline later back away from that given the silliness it produced and the backlash from the gaming community. Things that also seem &quot;so cool&quot; from the perspective of a single campaign at someone's table just looks ridiculous with perspective.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I think the mystery of the Maeljin Incarna is best explained that they are a rare breed of spectre.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:58:33-08:00","id":771792,"title":"","content":"And then there is sacrifying yourself when opening a closed caern (and having a chance to become its minor totem...). Well, that's for Were's usually, but it might be a way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9729,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9729-hira-akigi","user":"Hira Akigi","date":". 11-22-2015, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":